WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.775
Machine learning can only speed up antibody design
if models truly understand what makes an antibody good.

00:00:06.855 --> 00:00:11.172
Yet the major protein fitness benchmarks, like
CAFA, TAPE, and FLIP,

00:00:11.252 --> 00:00:15.764
either leave antibody data out entirely or include
only a sliver of it.

00:00:15.844 --> 00:00:21.260
That leaves researchers with no principled way to
check whether a deep learning model

00:00:21.340 --> 00:00:23.524
actually captures antibody fitness.

00:00:23.604 --> 00:00:28.827
Today the field often falls back on weak proxies
such as native sequence recovery,

00:00:28.907 --> 00:00:32.060
which say little about real therapeutic potential.
